  ('CTCT_SPCL_CARE_VARIANCE', 1, 'Special-care status carries more than one value', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_mock_ctct_c', 'SPCL_CARE_STTS', 'CDE_VULNERABLE_CUSTOMER', 'variance', '(SELECT count(DISTINCT SPCL_CARE_STTS) FROM {table}) <= 1', NULL, NULL, 0.0, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 'L2', 'active', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'A vulnerable-customer flag that is constant is almost certainly not being populated.'),
  ('CTCT_SPCL_CARE_VARIANCE', 2, 'Special-care status carries more than one value', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_mock_ctct_c', 'SPCL_CARE_STTS', 'CDE_VULNERABLE_CUSTOMER', 'variance', '(SELECT count(DISTINCT SPCL_CARE_STTS) FROM {table}) <= 1', NULL, NULL, 0.0, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 'L2', 'retired', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-01 09:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-10-01 09:00:00', 'j.tanaka@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'v2: retired 2026-10-01, with CDE_VULNERABLE_CUSTOMER. A count of distinct values cannot tell a defaulted flag from a population with no vulnerable customers, and failing it marked all 1000 rows. The runs before this date stand; nothing runs it after.'),
