  ('SUBS_MSISDN_SENTINEL', 1, 'Mobile service number is not a placeholder', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_mock_subs_c', 'PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT', 'CDE_CUST_MSISDN', 'sentinel', 'lower(trim(PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT)) IN (\'service-number-unknown\',\'unknown\',\'n/a\',\'na\',\'none\',\'null\',\'\')', NULL, 'PRIM_RSRC_TYPE_KEY = 1', 0.0, 'P1_block', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 'L2', 'active', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'v1 spelled the predicate out longhand. v2 calls dq.fn.is_sentinel_v1, the shared helper declared in sql/ddl/12_functions.sql. Identical counts on the same data -- sql/out/checkrun.sql was re-run against workspace.dq_triage before and after and every figure held. One definition instead of 1.'),
  ('SUBS_MSISDN_SENTINEL', 2, 'Mobile service number is not a placeholder', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_mock_subs_c', 'PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT', 'CDE_CUST_MSISDN', 'sentinel', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_fn_is_sentinel_v1(PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT)', NULL, 'PRIM_RSRC_TYPE_KEY = 1', 0.0, 'P1_block', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 'L2', 'active', TIMESTAMP '2026-07-19 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-07-19 03:00:00', 'j.tanaka@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-07-19 03:00:00', 'A live mobile service with no number is a provisioning gap, not a formatting nit.'),
  ('SUBS_MSISDN_FMT', 1, 'Mobile service number matches 04########', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_mock_subs_c', 'PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT', 'CDE_CUST_MSISDN', 'format', 'PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT NOT RLIKE \'^04[0-9]{8}$\'', NULL, NULL, 0.0, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 'L2', 'active', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'v1 had no scope_filter and reported 212 violations, 200 of which were Fixed Broadband service IDs in a different and correct format. Scoping to PRIM_RSRC_TYPE_KEY = 1 took it to 12 real ones. This is the fix COH-B is recommending for the two rules that still have the same defect.'),
  ('SUBS_MSISDN_FMT', 2, 'Mobile service number matches 04########', 'workspace.dq_triage.dq_mock_subs_c', 'PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT', 'CDE_CUST_MSISDN', 'format', 'PRIM_RSRC_VALU_TXT NOT RLIKE \'^04[0-9]{8}$\'', NULL, 'PRIM_RSRC_TYPE_KEY = 1', 0.0, 'P2_alert', 'Customer', 'dq-stewards-customer', 'L2', 'active', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'm.okonkwo@example.com', TIMESTAMP '2026-03-06 03:00:00', 'v2 spelled the predicate out longhand. v3 calls dq.fn.is_au_mobile_v1, the shared helper declared in sql/ddl/12_functions.sql -- the same concept CTCT_MOBL_FMT checks on another table under an unrelated column name, which is why naming it once matters. Identical counts: 12 on the same data, scope_filter untouched.'),
